{"name":"VIC 20 Green","hex":"#94e089","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Virgin Islands Creole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A victim of a homicide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vic"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"VIC-20","blocks":[{"text":"The VIC-20 is an 8-bit entry level home computer that was sold by Commodore Business Machines. The VIC-20 was announced in September 1980, roughly three years after Commodore's first personal computer, the PET. The VIC-20 was the first computer of any description to sell one million units, and sales of the VIC-20 eventually reached 2.5 million units."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Commodore-VIC-20-FL.jpg/330px-Commodore-VIC-20-FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VIC-20","wikidata":"Q918232"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/VIC-20_Display.jpg/500px-VIC-20_Display.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/VIC-20_Display.jpg/1280px-VIC-20_Display.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/VIC-20_Display.jpg/500px-VIC-20_Display.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An early revision of the VIC-20 with several accessories. The  composite output allowed it to be connected to standard television sets of its era.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVIC-20_Display.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/ViC20_Cartridge.jpg/330px-ViC20_Cartridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/ViC20_Cartridge.jpg/330px-ViC20_Cartridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Clowns game on a ROM cartridge","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AViC20_Cartridge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/VIC_20_Splash_Screen_Screenshot.gif/500px-VIC_20_Splash_Screen_Screenshot.gif?utm_source=